  AP Var(mu) = 2.8143; non-AP families with SMALLER Var: 400/400
  (AP is NOT the Var-minimizer)
  corr(Var(mu), safe) = +0.584 (does more variance => more safe/gap? the covering handle)

  ASSESSMENT: 2nd moment gives UPPER bounds on safe (Cauchy-Schwarz:
  Leb{mu>=1} >= E[mu]^2/E[mu^2]); it does NOT lower-bound safe (the
  density floor needs the full signed theta-series / Selberg minorant).
  BUT if the AP uniquely minimizes Var(mu), that is a fresh RIGIDITY
  handle (evenest-cover = equioscillation = AP), independent of safe.
